---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import TableDemo from "../../components/TableDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Table"
  description="Rows of records with sorting, filters, grouping, editing, and a card layout on phones."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Table</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    One table for every list of records. Pass rows and columns. Turn on the
    features you need: sorting, search and filter chips, group rows with totals,
    row edit, column layout, virtual rows, and row drag.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><TableDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Table usage"
      code={`import { Table, type TableColumn } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/table";

const columns: TableColumn<Order>[] = [
  { key: "customer", header: "Customer", sort: true, filter: "text" },
  { key: "crop", header: "Crop", filter: "select", group: true, options: crops },
  { key: "boxes", header: "Boxes", align: "right", sort: true, aggregate: "sum", edit: "number" },
];

<Table
  aria-label="Orders"
  data={orders}
  columns={columns}
  getRowId={(row) => row.id}
  searchable
  selectable
  onRowSave={(row, changes) => save(row.id, changes)}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>variant</code> is <code>"plain"</code> (default) or
      <code>"grid"</code>. Grid tables sit in a bordered scroll region capped at <code
        >60dvh</code
      >, with a pinned header. <code>narrow</code> is
      <code>"scroll"</code> (default) or <code>"stack"</code>, which turns rows
      into cards when the table is narrower than 36rem.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Columns</h2>
    <p>
      Each column reads <code>row[key]</code>. <code>cell</code> changes what shows,
      but sort, filter, and edit still use the raw value.
      <code>sort</code> adds a sort button. <code>filter</code> is
      <code>"text"</code>, <code>"number"</code>, <code>"select"</code>,
      <code>"date"</code>, or <code>"boolean"</code>. <code>edit</code> is
      <code>"text"</code>, <code>"number"</code>, <code>"select"</code>,
      <code>"date"</code>, or <code>"checkbox"</code>. <code>options</code>
      feeds select filters and editors. <code>group</code> lets people group by the
      column. <code>aggregate</code> (<code>"sum"</code>,
      <code>"count"</code>, <code>"min"</code>, <code>"max"</code>,
      <code>"mean"</code>) shows totals on group rows and in the footer.
      <code>hint</code> adds an info tooltip. <code>width</code>,
      <code>pin</code>, and <code>hidden</code> set the starting layout.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Rows</h2>
    <p>
      <code>getRowHref</code> or <code>onRowClick</code> turns the first cell into
      a link or button that covers the row. <code>actions</code> adds a pinned actions
      cell. <code>onRowSave</code> adds Edit, Save, and Cancel; if it rejects, the
      row stays open and shows the error.
      <code>selectable</code> adds checkboxes and calls
      <code>onSelectionChange</code> with row ids. Shift+click a checkbox to set every
      row since the last one picked. <code>getSubRows</code>
      nests rows. <code>onRowReorder</code> adds drag handles.
      <code>onRowDrop</code> accepts files dropped on a row.
      <code>pageSize</code> adds pages, and <code>virtual</code> draws only the rows
      in view. <code>loading</code> shows skeleton rows, and
      <code>empty</code> shows when no rows match.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">State and URLs</h2>
    <p>
      The table keeps its own state. Pass <code>state</code> to control any part,
      and <code>onStateChange</code> to hear every change. With
      <code>manual</code>, the server sorts, filters, and pages; pass
      <code>rowCount</code>. <code>persistKey</code> saves column widths, order, pinning,
      and visibility to localStorage.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Share the view in the URL"
      code={`import { useTableUrlState } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/table-nuqs";

const url = useTableUrlState({ prefix: "orders-" });

<Table aria-label="Orders" data={orders} columns={columns} getRowId={(row) => row.id} {...url} />`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>useTableUrlState</code> keeps sort, filters, search, grouping, and page
      in the URL with nuqs, so a shared link opens the same view. Install
      <code>nuqs</code> and add its adapter.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The table renders native <code>table</code> elements. Headings carry
      <code>aria-sort</code>. Checkboxes, editors, drag handles, and resize
      handles all work from the keyboard: drag handles use Space and the Arrow
      keys, and resize handles use the Arrow keys. Group rows use
      <code>aria-expanded</code>. Virtual rows set <code>aria-rowcount</code>
      and <code>aria-rowindex</code>. The stack layout keeps table roles and
      labels each value with its column name.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Row dividers use <code>--sprout-line</code>; grid dividers and the frame
      use <code>--sprout-input</code>. Hover and grid header tints are
      <code>--sprout-table-hover</code> and <code>--sprout-table-head-bg</code>.
      Selected rows use <code>--sprout-primary-subtle</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
